In article <walker.744190641@mits> walker@mits.mdata.fi (Jukka Lahtinen) writes:
>wart@cco.caltech.edu (Michael L. Thomas) writes:
>
>>my ghost started attacking me in the shop.  No biggie, except that the
>>shopkeeper apparently didn't think I was dead and also started attacking
>>me.  So I'm standing in the door with a ghost and a shopkeeper hitting me.
>>Why??  How can I avoid this?  Would the same thing happen if it had been
>>someone else's ghost?
>
>You guessed it. The shopkeeper in the bones file still remembers the name
>of the player who robbed his shop. If you had been using another name, the
>shopkeeper wouldn't have been angry to you, he would have just said
>"Hello A, I'm looking for B" (where A is your name now, and B is the name
>of the player who robbed the shop). And I believe this happens in every
>version of hack/nethack.

Almost correct.  In version 1.0.2, shopkeepers don't try to kill you if
you rob the shop.  They just follow at your heels, up and down staircases
too, demanding payment.  You either have to pay them, kill them, teleport
away, or walk into another shop and put on a ring of conflict.  Or due to 
a bug in the code, if you go back in to the original shop and pay the 
shopkeeper any amount of gold (even if it doesn't cover the bill), the 
bill will be paid in full.

So, if the shopkeeper in the bones file attacked the new player, it was
because the old player of the same name and class attacked and was killed
by the shopkeeper in the previous game.  Just robbing the store wouldn't
be enough.

Anyways, killing shopkeepers in 1.0.2 should not be attempted until you're
coming back up with the amulet.  It destroys your luck, which makes all the
wands of wishing you get on the hell levels non-functional.

